At 04:44 PM 4/30/04 -0700, Jorge "Llambías" wrote:
>--- Robin Lee Powell <rlpowell@digitalkingdom.org> wrote:
> > On Fri, Apr 30, 2004 at 03:40:01PM -0700, Jorge Llamb?as wrote:
> >
> > > Capitalizing the whole syllable doesn't look very nice anyway,
> >
> > In your opinion.
>
>In my opinion it looks horrible. I wonder if anyone really thinks
>it looks very nice.

You should be able to guess that I adopted the practice because I thought 
it looks nice.  I prefer it to the two alternate methods I've seen for 
showing stress (an accent mark before - or after - the syllable in 
question, and capitalizing only the vowel, which looks to me like someone 
doing word-art, and I sometimes don't notice the capitalization)

> > > and there are no fixed rules in Lojban for syllable break-up.
> >
> > There aren't?
>
>Are there?

I believe we specified rules back in the original morphology paper (which 
predates Lojban, being a modified version of a paper about TLI Loglan), but 
I don't know if they made it into the red book.

